      "message": "I haven\u0027t done a deep review of the python side, but the logic sgtm!\n\nI\u0027m a bit on the fence on using the FQDN as cluster group name, \"drmrs01\" for example seems cleaner), the FQDN could maybe be a custom field.\n\nIf I understand correctly there must be some puppet code first to define profile_config[\u0027site\u0027] in the config file.\nI also think that you\u0027re not using the \"api\" line from the config file and use the \"cluster\" one instead, but I fail to see where you\u0027re setting the port to 5080.\n\nOther than that I think this is great to add the feature to the existing script without changing the behavior much.\n\nA different approach, maybe for a latter iteration would be that the cluster groups are defined authoritatively in Netbox (manually, as they don\u0027t change often), then the script uses the Netbox data to find which endpoint to query to populate the cluster. Moving the source of truth to Netbox instead in having it in the config file.",
